{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/597613-beasts-as-demon-antagonists","id":597613,"title":"Beasts as Demon Antagonists","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-20T18:42:35-07:00","id":597613,"title":"Beasts as Demon Antagonists","content":"Partly since I'm waiting for the STG to give me new Numina, partly because I think the atavisms and nightmares are pretty cool, but mostly because they come of as so <i>smug</i> (read the Beast stereotypes section) I want to use a Beast as an antagonist in a Demon game.<br /> <br /> Has anyone else tried this yet? Any advice to share?<br /> <br /> Any insight or input on using them in a Demon chronicle?<br /> <br /> And now that I think about it, they would be very fitting for the Biblical Era shard. &quot;Giants in the Earth&quot; indeed... <br /> <br /> (and please limit any complaints about BtP, we already have a raging firestorm out in the general forum...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T20:03:48-07:00","id":597718,"title":"","content":"They'd present a good opponent that would make working with the God Machine's agents seem potentially appealing. Considering the mandated antagonistic relationship between God-machine products and Beasts, Demons and Angels teaming up to deal with one would actually be pretty plausible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T22:56:06-07:00","id":597890,"title":"","content":"Beasts are pretty easy to include as antagonists in a demon game. <br /> <br /> Technically, the book only says that demons don't count as kin, it says nothing about stigmatics, hellblooded, cryptids, or even angels as far as I recall.<br /> <br /> So Beasts can show up as the master of a pack of feral cryptids, the benefactor of a stigmatic a demon might want to make into a resource, the friend of a demon's kid that tries to convince the kid to break ties with the demon, or an angel's wingman. <br /> <br /> Other ideas are that ghosts and spirits count as kin, so a demon who goes around skinning ephemerals for ephemeral covers might annoy a beast.<br /> <br /> Beasts investigate urban legends, demons are known for creating urban legends, well natural enmity can take it from there. <br /> <br /> Local infrastructure might be in the physical location a beast makes a chamber on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T11:08:08-07:00","id":598551,"title":"","content":"Think it'll be like Planescape, with DtD representing the Devils of the Nine Hells, and Beast equating to the Demons of the Abyss?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T22:24:38-07:00","id":599039,"title":"","content":"Id personally read the fluff that beasts wouldn't count any GM product as kin, but they could certainly make great antagonists as the characters try to move outside of GM influence, or as the beasts manifest near covers and start hurting people around the demon, leading towards investigations by heroes stripping away cover...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5718-hackthulhu","name":"Hackthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T05:00:56-07:00","id":599211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/597613-beasts-as-demon-antagonists?p=597718#post597718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They'd present a good opponent that would make working with the God Machine's agents seem potentially appealing. Considering the mandated antagonistic relationship between God-machine products and Beasts, Demons and Angels teaming up to deal with one would actually be pretty plausible.</div> </div> </div> </div> its not mandated. In fact, when the Beast and Unchained meet, and the Unchained wins the contest? The Begotten gets the Leveraged Condition, which means the demon has an advantage over the Beast to do... Something. <br /> <br /> <br /> Beasts are, in a very real way, anti-hunters. But, where hunters are predisposed to hunting other supers, beasts are predisposed to helping. Yes, you can't establish Kinship, and the initial meeting is tense, but that doesn't imply antagonism. Demons tend to freak out around Beasts because of the automatic potential to break Cover. Once they do? The demon gets suspicious from their Cover being shaken OR they get info to use against tHe Beast - the Demons have the advantage to befriend them, believe it or not.<br /> <br /> Actually, I will have to look it up, but are Unchained excluded from that initial Good Impression? I don't recall.<br /> <br /> Anyways, I just wanted to point out some considerations. Nothing stops a beast from being friends with the ring's enemies, or something else. There's a lot of potential here beyond just foes, for instance. One could conclude that beasts and their Dark Mother are anti-angels and could provide a path to Hell. <br /> <br /> Definitely intesting to have, with a lot of potential misunderstandings","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T06:19:37-07:00","id":600526,"title":"","content":"A christain beast who doesn't know how to deal with his deal with what he is and his belief. He teams up with angels (not in a kinship) to hunt demons to cause fear. They are just machines, spirits or a mix or something. No one is reall getting hurt. Much better than harming humans he once belong to. Strange that he get full though. At first he thought it was the hunt but that not it. He needs to feast on fear. The thing is the demons can't be afaird can they? They sure do not show it (unless they want to). Unless they want to... There is no way they are feeling real fear can they? Nah their progaming must be so good that their acting must be real. Yeah that what it is.<br /> <br /> Or even better a beast trying to make new kin starts to burn the players cover because he wants to find them and make friends. He is looking in the wrong places and talking to the wrong people as a demon would see it. He would be an antagonist but not a bad person. Do you kill him before he ends up calling all angels? Make allies knowing he does not understand the great threat of the God-Machine? Or send him after some demons you are not to friendly with hoping that the beast will end up dead and the demon will be on the run without a cover?<br /> <br /> The thing is you want the beast to be human (or at least be human once). The best villains are the ones that once you stop them and find out their plan, you find out that in their head they are doing good, or that they are the same as the players but on a different side. Maybe someone they loved got soul pacted, G-M have brain washed them.<br /> <br /> Like the example I gave the players could turn this person into an ally. They could gve him something bigger to fight (the G-M and his cultists) or they can end up trying to kill each other.<br /> An antagonist is only an antagonist out of circomestance. They are a person too. <br /> Are they getting in the players way?<br /> Hunting the demon players? (what would be great if they hunt the demon player thinking they are human)<br /> On different sides of a war?<br /> <br /> What is important is that you do not just make them into a monster of the week. That they are not Evil(tm). Do not make it easy for the players to kill the beast.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4090-mental-state","name":"Mental-State","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T06:44:55-07:00","id":600538,"title":"","content":"Another thing you really should consider: Demons are spies, so that means that they are on the look out for assets to recruit and subvert. We have an entire agenda (Tempters) that specialize in seducing someone to the &quot;dark side.&quot; Messengers especially have a lot of tricks to get someone on their side. If one of the PCs are going to be a Tempter Trumpet, then you should be prepared to have someone looking to make the Beast an ally instead of enemy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T07:03:38-07:00","id":600547,"title":"","content":"Yeah that was my point, in WoD you all play monsters. You villian can become your best friend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4090-mental-state","name":"Mental-State","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T08:52:56-07:00","id":600599,"title":"","content":"I'm still waiting to see if and/or how they'll tie it all into Inferno.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T00:08:43-07:00","id":606402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/597613-beasts-as-demon-antagonists?p=600599#post600599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still waiting to see if and/or how they'll tie it all into Inferno.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's pretty much written in the Corebook? Descent demons have nothing to do with Inferno and both of these can coexist.. along any number of other creatures who are called &quot;demons&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}